[[:db/retract 17592186124884 :question/answer-fields 17592186121904] {:db/id 17592186124477 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c6f93be2-7ce6-5b4b-af0d-5674ab7e6429" "question-a184c001-bd4f-576e-9731-bffadf7bf486"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124290 :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its pivot columns?\n![](images/ce/ce4c17b3e47f0618d315e8e61feeb2b58cd913e54b63a3a375b8bd4676efbc8e.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](images/31/31b76b7840d750cf7cf060c5d218644f8733d46a0b59c0e347aeb634ea6c1091.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124478 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124291 :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $C$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n![](images/b1/b1f927457c74f57ff2e7cdb9d030492fffcb49bdfd9199e8720d3da2263e0b1e.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $C$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n![](images/05/05264585d59a4430f5424b91f649eecc80a5f28fa460a935f5c224882e08d56c.svg)\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124479 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7b4a741d-30d4-5d2c-9fde-2ae106aac7d2"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124292 :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $A,$ given by\n![](images/df/dfe650778e528254fc2098714566d954c47442ede485d6a92495cf16eb9e936d.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124293 :question/problem "What are the pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n![](images/f1/f10a5ef881920312ccdb163d9db70779d3848f7dc510c29d516eaf74a5ddd38d.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-c6f93be2-7ce6-5b4b-af0d-5674ab7e6429" :question/id #uuid "c6f93be2-7ce6-5b4b-af0d-5674ab7e6429" :question/math-academy-id "q-73610" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $M$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $M?$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $M$ has $3$ pivots in the $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-88d3331d-a8e6-536c-a68d-cb0f9e32a075"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-88d3331d-a8e6-536c-a68d-cb0f9e32a075" :answer-field/id #uuid "88d3331d-a8e6-536c-a68d-cb0f9e32a075" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-28bfa91c-82e1-5695-aab6-f95656dc0054" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c83b88d1-5d2c-5736-8274-209a5fbf1ac9" "answer-535d0a87-47c8-56ec-b2b5-e67c0a120f70" "answer-e0e3cec8-fcda-5297-8c84-5312b9c33501" "answer-28bfa91c-82e1-5695-aab6-f95656dc0054" "answer-8eb34693-58c1-5d7d-86b0-1c33b73b83c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c83b88d1-5d2c-5736-8274-209a5fbf1ac9" :answer/id #uuid "c83b88d1-5d2c-5736-8274-209a5fbf1ac9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-535d0a87-47c8-56ec-b2b5-e67c0a120f70" :answer/id #uuid "535d0a87-47c8-56ec-b2b5-e67c0a120f70" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e0e3cec8-fcda-5297-8c84-5312b9c33501" :answer/id #uuid "e0e3cec8-fcda-5297-8c84-5312b9c33501" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-28bfa91c-82e1-5695-aab6-f95656dc0054" :answer/id #uuid "28bfa91c-82e1-5695-aab6-f95656dc0054" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8eb34693-58c1-5d7d-86b0-1c33b73b83c5" :answer/id #uuid "8eb34693-58c1-5d7d-86b0-1c33b73b83c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd, $4$th, and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a184c001-bd4f-576e-9731-bffadf7bf486" :question/id #uuid "a184c001-bd4f-576e-9731-bffadf7bf486" :question/math-academy-id "q-35451" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $A?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-78144882-efa2-5484-a8c1-a8247fae02ff"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-78144882-efa2-5484-a8c1-a8247fae02ff" :answer-field/id #uuid "78144882-efa2-5484-a8c1-a8247fae02ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-986560a5-e5d7-5f97-aa00-b1dbaa8f20a4" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6b995835-5cad-5c17-9907-2c811946d492" "answer-ac4622be-bec1-5fc1-8091-18785690fe53" "answer-dd3451e3-4afd-5c54-a3fa-5deb8c8c1152" "answer-986560a5-e5d7-5f97-aa00-b1dbaa8f20a4" "answer-278b166f-4613-50ce-a51a-4330a87230e8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6b995835-5cad-5c17-9907-2c811946d492" :answer/id #uuid "6b995835-5cad-5c17-9907-2c811946d492" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac4622be-bec1-5fc1-8091-18785690fe53" :answer/id #uuid "ac4622be-bec1-5fc1-8091-18785690fe53" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd3451e3-4afd-5c54-a3fa-5deb8c8c1152" :answer/id #uuid "dd3451e3-4afd-5c54-a3fa-5deb8c8c1152" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-986560a5-e5d7-5f97-aa00-b1dbaa8f20a4" :answer/id #uuid "986560a5-e5d7-5f97-aa00-b1dbaa8f20a4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$1$st, $3$rd, and $5$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-278b166f-4613-50ce-a51a-4330a87230e8" :answer/id #uuid "278b166f-4613-50ce-a51a-4330a87230e8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "All the columns are pivot" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" :question/id #uuid "ef768962-c254-565f-ad90-7c7187cd37b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-73613" :question/problem "The row echelon form matrix $B$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $B$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $2$nd column." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-846e9557-c707-56d2-86ec-10035a40ea93"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-846e9557-c707-56d2-86ec-10035a40ea93" :answer-field/id #uuid "846e9557-c707-56d2-86ec-10035a40ea93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-82e06dac-e13b-51bb-b072-e0b02f1d17f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-3c750eaf-692f-5572-bdcf-255079d52728" "answer-439cc40e-3b18-56fc-b431-aca3fb7a238d" "answer-82e06dac-e13b-51bb-b072-e0b02f1d17f0" "answer-ceaf59cb-72f9-5884-b2ae-369f981d4b01" "answer-cf412197-e968-5ab2-9ca2-3bedc14b3ab0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3c750eaf-692f-5572-bdcf-255079d52728" :answer/id #uuid "3c750eaf-692f-5572-bdcf-255079d52728" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd and $3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-439cc40e-3b18-56fc-b431-aca3fb7a238d" :answer/id #uuid "439cc40e-3b18-56fc-b431-aca3fb7a238d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd and $4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82e06dac-e13b-51bb-b072-e0b02f1d17f0" :answer/id #uuid "82e06dac-e13b-51bb-b072-e0b02f1d17f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$2$nd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ceaf59cb-72f9-5884-b2ae-369f981d4b01" :answer/id #uuid "ceaf59cb-72f9-5884-b2ae-369f981d4b01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3$rd only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cf412197-e968-5ab2-9ca2-3bedc14b3ab0" :answer/id #uuid "cf412197-e968-5ab2-9ca2-3bedc14b3ab0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4$th only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124884 :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6f646bf1-b053-51af-98e8-66196b742893"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6f646bf1-b053-51af-98e8-66196b742893" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f646bf1-b053-51af-98e8-66196b742893" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4fd90c1d-53e5-5f45-8848-752538c1d508" :answer-field/choices ["answer-442b7450-7d3f-5b57-8244-47e2ea21ed79" "answer-0bf2fc69-40c7-50ed-b76f-0a01f02146c1" "answer-4fd90c1d-53e5-5f45-8848-752538c1d508" "answer-c5092969-970d-5cce-acd5-6e2221c79fa7" "answer-4fbea88a-54a4-589b-953c-572e039364e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-442b7450-7d3f-5b57-8244-47e2ea21ed79" :answer/id #uuid "442b7450-7d3f-5b57-8244-47e2ea21ed79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0bf2fc69-40c7-50ed-b76f-0a01f02146c1" :answer/id #uuid "0bf2fc69-40c7-50ed-b76f-0a01f02146c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fd90c1d-53e5-5f45-8848-752538c1d508" :answer/id #uuid "4fd90c1d-53e5-5f45-8848-752538c1d508" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5092969-970d-5cce-acd5-6e2221c79fa7" :answer/id #uuid "c5092969-970d-5cce-acd5-6e2221c79fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4fbea88a-54a4-589b-953c-572e039364e6" :answer/id #uuid "4fbea88a-54a4-589b-953c-572e039364e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-7b4a741d-30d4-5d2c-9fde-2ae106aac7d2" :question/id #uuid "7b4a741d-30d4-5d2c-9fde-2ae106aac7d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-130961" :question/problem "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $P,$ given by\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to convert $P$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{4} & :={R}_{4}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $P$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-76643a29-5807-570f-8aa9-f5fb774e145b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-76643a29-5807-570f-8aa9-f5fb774e145b" :answer-field/id #uuid "76643a29-5807-570f-8aa9-f5fb774e145b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c25b5ef-b912-5c71-9670-944d65285749" "answer-fa159688-f836-5d57-8c3c-4060d2af4504" "answer-ad1a92a6-f6d8-5aa2-9a4c-0f2edb4ce9bc" "answer-e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" "answer-f3c840b3-dbab-5742-a2b1-8a2edee0b393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c25b5ef-b912-5c71-9670-944d65285749" :answer/id #uuid "2c25b5ef-b912-5c71-9670-944d65285749" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa159688-f836-5d57-8c3c-4060d2af4504" :answer/id #uuid "fa159688-f836-5d57-8c3c-4060d2af4504" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad1a92a6-f6d8-5aa2-9a4c-0f2edb4ce9bc" :answer/id #uuid "ad1a92a6-f6d8-5aa2-9a4c-0f2edb4ce9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" :answer/id #uuid "e884e7e6-8f56-5bfb-a2ca-b9c4594a1a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3c840b3-dbab-5742-a2b1-8a2edee0b393" :answer/id #uuid "f3c840b3-dbab-5742-a2b1-8a2edee0b393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125757 :tutorial/content "The **pivots** of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nFor example, given the matrix \n![](images/ad/addf5cd1e1219a1e1ce28f3d27d1b000b3a99640ff89a62e55b66f3a5cdb3521.svg)\nwhich is in row echelon form, let's find the pivots of $A.$\n\n- The first non-zero entry in the first row is the entry $a_{11}=1.$ So this is a pivot.\n\n- The first non-zero entry of the second row is $a_{22}=1.$ So this is also a pivot.\n\n- The first non-zero entry in the third row is $a_{34}=1.$ Therefore this is a pivot.\n\nThe pivots of $A$ are highlighted below.\n\n![](images/96/96dcf8cf9f0d387e0539ea04dd7ae4a498534361ad6bd5ed3bb119ae21f0416a.svg)\n\nThe **pivot columns** of a matrix in row echelon form are simply the columns in which the pivots appear.\n\nFor our matrix $A$, we can see that the pivot columns are the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th columns.\n\nThe non-pivot columns are the columns that do not contain a pivot. So for the matrix $A,$ the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124704 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
